/// DERIVED, not published: each plan row spread over periods 1 to 12 by a share taken from the prior year's outturn (or twelve flat twelfths where there is none). The monthly plan is my allocation of a published annual figure; the twelve rows of a plan row add up to it exactly. Scenario is Plan (phased), which is flagged derived. It never enters a real total and must never be shown as a published monthly budget. Source view dw.v_model_fact_plan_phased.
table 'Fact Plan Phased (derived)'
	lineageTag: 5062fe90-72fd-53c1-b03e-fbb10cb1df39

	/// DERIVED, not published: the plan rows that Plan adds up, spread over periods 1 to 12 by a share taken from the prior year's outturn (twelve flat twelfths where there is none), in GBP thousands. The only plan measure allowed at month grain. The twelve months of a plan row add up to the published annual figure exactly, but the monthly figures are my allocation and must never be shown as a published monthly budget. BLANK below the group grain (sub-segment, economic category and so on) like Plan, and for FY2017-18, which has no calendar.
	measure 'Plan (phased)' =
			IF (
			    Grain.BelowGrain ( TRUE () ),
			    BLANK (),
			    VAR PlanKeys =
			        SELECTCOLUMNS (
			            Plan.RowsInScope (
			                ISFILTERED ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] ) || ISFILTERED ( 'Fact Plan Phased (derived)'[Plan Measure] )
			            ),
			            "k", 'Fact Plan'[Plan Fact Key]
			        )
			    RETURN
			        CALCULATE (
			            SUM ( 'Fact Plan Phased (derived)'[Phased Amount] ),
			            TREATAS ( PlanKeys, 'Fact Plan Phased (derived)'[Plan Fact Key] )
			        )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan\Derived
		lineageTag: 0260e1e9-08ca-5ae8-96c5-5321d21ed6c7

	/// DERIVED, not published: outturn on the plan's basis less the phased plan, GBP thousands, in the period context (a month, or the year to date under Time Intelligence). The plan side is my allocation of a published annual plan, so the figure is a variance to my profile and not to a published monthly budget. Below zero is favourable with spending positive. BLANK where either side is BLANK, including below the group grain.
	measure 'Variance to Phased Plan' =
			VAR Actual = [Outturn (plan basis)]
			VAR PhasedPlan = [Plan (phased)]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( Actual ) || ISBLANK ( PhasedPlan ), BLANK (), Actual - PhasedPlan )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan\Derived
		lineageTag: 15cb7749-8b1b-5e1f-a17d-c28800e63cc7

	/// DERIVED, not published: the variance to the phased plan as a share of the absolute phased plan. BLANK where the phased plan is zero or either side is BLANK.
	measure 'Variance to Phased Plan %' =
			VAR Actual = [Outturn (plan basis)]
			VAR PhasedPlan = [Plan (phased)]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( Actual ) || ISBLANK ( PhasedPlan ), BLANK (), DIVIDE ( Actual - PhasedPlan, ABS ( PhasedPlan ) ) )
		formatString: 0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%
		displayFolder: Plan\Derived
		lineageTag: 0fc9b425-f69f-5aae-bbd4-c3c9b28bf612

	/// DERIVED, not published: the phased plan is my allocation of the published annual plan. [Plan (phased)] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Plan (phased) (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Plan (phased)] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: 65842436-f90d-4dde-a019-e006123abce5

